<title>USA: Eaton Vance says Hawkes to become president.</title>
<headline>Eaton Vance says Hawkes to become president.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eaton Vance Corp said on Monday that it named James Hawkes as president and chief executive officer, effective November 1, 1996.</p>
<p>Hawkes, executive vice president, succeeds M. Dozier Gardner, who will become vice chairman of Eaton Vance, a Boston-based investment management firm.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
